2	//! Location service layer.
3	//!
4	//! This module abstracts platform-specific geolocation sources behind a common
5	//! `LocationProvider` trait, converts raw coordinates into domain events, and
6	//! forwards them through the global `EventBus` so that the rest of the
7	//! application can react (palette generation, analytics, etc.).
8	//!
9	//! Architectural notes
10	//! -------------------
11	//! • Factory Pattern    – `LocationProviderFactory` produces the best available
12	//!   provider at runtime (GPS, fused, mock, …).
13	//! • Singleton          – `LocationService::instance()` exposes a single,
14	//!   lazily-initialised service shared across the app.
15	//! • Observer Pattern   – events are dispatched through `EventBus`. Any number
16	//!   of observers (analytics, crash reporting, UI view-models) may subscribe
17	//!   without coupling to this module.
18	//! • Async / Tokio      – location streams are processed on a background task,
19	//!   leaving UI threads free.
20	//!
21	//! The implementation purposefully remains platform-agnostic; real iOS /
22	//! Android providers can be dropped in behind `cfg` flags without touching the
23	//! public surface.
24	
