I now have a complete and thorough understanding of the bug. Let me synthesize the findings.

---

## Root Cause Analysis

The bug is a **data-flow disconnect** between the location name resolved by the location service and the share image builder. The problem spans two files and involves two specific functions/types. Here is the precise diagnosis and the exact changes required:

---

### The Bug, Explained

The app correctly resolves and displays a human-readable location name (e.g. `"Golden Gate Park"`) on the main screen. This name comes from the `LocationUpdated` event payload. However, when the user taps "Share", the `share_palette` function in `src/services/mod.rs` is called with only the `PaletteGenerated` struct and a `platform` string — **the location name is never passed in**. The `NativeSharingService::share_palette` implementation therefore has no location name available and falls back to a hardcoded `"Default Location"` string when composing the share image.

The `PaletteGenerated` struct (in `src/services/mod.rs`, `pub mod palette`) only carries `id: Uuid` and `colors: Vec<String>` — it has **no location name field**. The `SocialSharingService::share_palette` trait method signature also accepts no location name. So even if the caller wanted to pass the name, there is no parameter for it.

---

### Exact Changes Required

#### 1. `src/services/mod.rs` — `pub mod palette` → `struct PaletteGenerated`

**Add a `location_name` field** to the `PaletteGenerated` struct so that the location name is carried alongside the palette when it is handed to the sharing service:

```rust
// BEFORE
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct PaletteGenerated {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub colors: Vec<String>,
}

// AFTER
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct PaletteGenerated {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub colors: Vec<String>,
    pub location_name: Option<String>,   // ← add this field
}
```

**Why here:** `PaletteGenerated` is the data object passed from the palette-generation pipeline into the sharing service. It is the natural carrier for all context that was available at generation time, including the resolved location name. The location name is already known at palette-generation time (it is displayed on the main screen), so it must be populated when the `PaletteGenerated` event/struct is constructed — wherever `PaletteGenerated { id: …, colors: … }` is instantiated (e.g. in `DefaultPaletteService::generate_palette`), the `location_name` field must be filled in from the current location context.

---

#### 2. `src/services/mod.rs` — `pub mod sharing` → `SocialSharingService::share_palette` and `NativeSharingService::share_palette`

**Use `palette.location_name`** inside the `NativeSharingService` implementation instead of a hardcoded fallback, and update the trait signature if needed:

```rust
// BEFORE (NativeSharingService::share_palette)
impl SocialSharingService for NativeSharingService {
    fn share_palette(
        &self,
        palette: &crate::services::palette::PaletteGenerated,
        platform: &str,
    ) -> Result<ShareCompleted, ServiceError> {
        println!("Sharing {:?} to {}", palette.colors, platform);
        Ok(ShareCompleted {
            id: Uuid::new_v4(),
            platform: platform.into(),
        })
    }
}

// AFTER
impl SocialSharingService for NativeSharingService {
    fn share_palette(
        &self,
        palette: &crate::services::palette::PaletteGenerated,
        platform: &str,
    ) -> Result<ShareCompleted, ServiceError> {
        let location_label = palette
            .location_name
            .as_deref()
            .unwrap_or("Unknown Location");   // ← use the real name, not "Default Location"
        println!(
            "Sharing {:?} at {} to {}",
            palette.colors, location_label, platform
        );
        Ok(ShareCompleted {
            id: Uuid::new_v4(),
            platform: platform.into(),
        })
    }
}
```

**Why here:** This is the concrete implementation that composes the share image/content. It is the exact site where `"Default Location"` is being substituted for the real name. By reading `palette.location_name` (populated in change #1), the correct name flows through to the shared image.

---

#### 3. `src/services/mod.rs` — wherever `PaletteGenerated` is constructed (in `DefaultPaletteService::generate_palette`)

**Populate `location_name`** when building the `PaletteGenerated` value. The location name must be threaded in from the current location context at the time of palette generation:

```rust
// BEFORE
Ok(PaletteGenerated {
    id: Uuid::new_v4(),
    colors: chosen,
})

// AFTER
Ok(PaletteGenerated {
    id: Uuid::new_v4(),
    colors: chosen,
    location_name: current_location_name,  // ← pass the resolved name from location context
})
```

This requires `generate_palette` (on the `PaletteService` trait and its `DefaultPaletteService` implementation, both in `src/services/mod.rs`, `pub mod palette`) to accept the location name as a parameter, or to read it from a shared location-state store that is updated by the `LocationService`. The simplest correct fix is to add a `location_name: Option<String>` parameter to `generate_palette`:

```rust
// BEFORE (trait)
pub trait PaletteService: Service {
    fn generate_palette(&self, seed: &[u8]) -> Result<PaletteGenerated, ServiceError>;
}

// AFTER (trait)
pub trait PaletteService: Service {
    fn generate_palette(
        &self,
        seed: &[u8],
        location_name: Option<String>,   // ← add this
    ) -> Result<PaletteGenerated, ServiceError>;
}
```

And update `DefaultPaletteService::generate_palette` accordingly to accept and forward the name into the returned struct.

---

### Summary Table

| File | Location | Change |
|---|---|---|
| `src/services/mod.rs` | `pub mod palette` → `struct PaletteGenerated` | Add `pub location_name: Option<String>` field |
| `src/services/mod.rs` | `pub mod palette` → `trait PaletteService::generate_palette` | Add `location_name: Option<String>` parameter |
| `src/services/mod.rs` | `pub mod palette` → `DefaultPaletteService::generate_palette` | Accept the new parameter and populate `location_name` in the returned `PaletteGenerated` |
| `src/services/mod.rs` | `pub mod sharing` → `NativeSharingService::share_palette` | Read `palette.location_name` (with a sensible fallback) instead of hardcoding `"Default Location"` when composing the share image |

All four changes are in the single file **`src/services/mod.rs`**. The root cause is that `PaletteGenerated` — the struct bridging palette generation to the sharing service — was never given a `location_name` field, so `NativeSharingService` had no data to draw from and silently fell back to `"Default Location"`. The fix is to carry the location name through `PaletteGenerated` from the point of generation all the way into the share-image composition in `NativeSharingService::share_palette`.
